From: mix2-port <mix2@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: qcom-labibb: optionally keep the PMIC default voltage

On LCD phones the downstream driver (qcom,qpnp-{lab,ibb}-use-default-voltage)
clears the voltage override bit, so LAB and IBB run at the output voltage
the PMIC is configured for, and the display driver never sets a voltage.
Add a qcom,use-default-voltage property that does the same at probe time,
so the Xiaomi Mi MIX 2 JDI panel keeps the bias it runs at from the
bootloader instead of a guessed override voltage.
---
 drivers/regulator/qcom-labibb-regulator.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/regulator/qcom-labibb-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/qcom-labibb-regulator.c
@@ -831,6 +831,20 @@ static int qcom_labibb_regulator_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		irq = of_irq_get_byname(reg_node, "ocp");
 		vreg->ocp_irq = irq;
 		vreg->ocp_irq_count = 0;
+
+		/*
+		 * Run at the PMIC's default output voltage like downstream does;
+		 * the voltage read back afterwards is meaningless.
+		 */
+		if (of_property_read_bool(reg_node, "qcom,use-default-voltage")) {
+			ret = regmap_update_bits(reg_regmap, reg_data->desc->vsel_reg,
+						 reg_data->desc->vsel_mask |
+						 LABIBB_VOLTAGE_OVERRIDE_EN, 0);
+			if (ret < 0) {
+				of_node_put(reg_node);
+				return ret;
+			}
+		}
 		of_node_put(reg_node);
 
 		vreg->regmap = reg_regmap;
